# Marketing Consulting Kit — working notes

## What this repo is
Prompt packs (`prompts/`) plus a small runner (`run_prompt.py`) that calls any
OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Deliverables are graded by humans via `EVALUATION.md`;
the code only moves a filled prompt to a model and prints the reply.

## Commands (source of truth — don't duplicate here)
- Flags & usage: `python run_prompt.py --help`
- Setup & examples: `README.md` Quick start
- In short: `--provider auto` (default) picks `claude` when `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` is set,
  else the `freellmapi` gateway. `--dry-run` prints the resolved request and makes no call.

## Testing
- Offline, no keys: `pip install -r requirements-dev.txt && pytest -q`
- CI runs the same on push/PR (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`).
- Keep tests offline: use an in-process mock server, never a real endpoint or key.
- Verify any provider change in order: `--dry-run` → local mock → real key.

## Model IDs (Claude drifts over time)
- Defaults live in `CLAUDE_MODELS` in `run_prompt.py`; override with `--model` or
  `CLAUDE_MODEL_SMART|BALANCED|FAST`.
- If a model id is rejected, discover valid ones and retry with `--model`:
  `client.models.list()` against `https://api.anthropic.com/v1/` using `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`.

## Gotchas / lessons
- Keep `--dry-run` and `--list-profiles` dependency-free: import `openai` lazily,
  only inside the live request path.
- Python: declare `global` before first use — a `global`-after-use `SyntaxError`
  previously made the whole script fail to launch.
- Dev environment is just Python 3.12 + `openai` (`requirements.txt`); install with
  `pip install --user -r requirements.txt`.

## Before committing
- [ ] `pytest -q` passes
- [ ] `python run_prompt.py --dry-run --profile ad-copy --text "x"` still prints (no import/syntax break)
- [ ] no keys or secrets in the diff (see the always-on `secrets` rule)
